derivations.claim:
[Sufficiency of the criterion] Assume $M_{b}M_{a}=0$ for $b
e a$ and $F_{a}^{2}=F_{a}$ whenever $F_{a}
e0$. Fix a state $ho$ and $a$ with $p_{a}>0$, and let $ho_{a}$ be the conditional state. Then $p_{a}=\operatorname{tr}(ho F_{a})>0$ forces $F_{a}
e0$, and the probability that the immediate repetition returns $a$ is $\operatorname{tr}(ho_{a}F_{a})=\operatorname{tr}(M_{a}ho M_{a}^{*}F_{a})/p_{a}=\operatorname{tr}(ho M_{a}^{*}F_{a}M_{a})/p_{a}=\operatorname{tr}(ho F_{a}^{2})/p_{a}=\operatorname{tr}(ho F_{a})/p_{a}=1$, using $M_{a}^{*}F_{a}M_{a}=M_{a}^{*}M_{a}^{*}M_{a}M_{a}=(F_{a})^{2}$ and [F5]. For $b
e a$, $\operatorname{tr}(ho_{a}F_{b})=\operatorname{tr}(ho M_{a}^{*}M_{b}^{*}M_{b}M_{a})/p_{a}=\operatorname{tr}(ho (M_{b}M_{a})^{*}(M_{b}M_{a}))/p_{a}=0$ by $M_{b}M_{a}=0$. Hence the instrument is repeatable. [step 2.1, given, F1, F5, algebra]
